                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "- It's all about the timer. If you have ADHD or want to relax, this won't do at all. \n- The interface is hard to understand (the button to go back from one menu to another is a red pool). \n+ The assets and souds are pretty, but that's it. \n+ There are some nice gameplay ideas. \n\nBut that can't make up for these basic function that's missing: \n- The audio settings are only acessible from the start page, and you can't change how loud the music is.\n- The audio preference (on/off for music only) is not saved and reset everytime you start a level.\nUnless the game get an update that fix these basic features, I can't recommend it. \nOtherwise, I'd say, if you don't have any word game, I'd say go for it.",
